 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0,
   "end": 1.27,
   "text": "The blackout is over."
  },
  {
   "start": 1.61,
   "end": 2.58,
   "text": "The lights are back."
  },
  {
   "start": 2.95,
   "end": 3.67,
   "text": "And this..."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.93,
   "end": 5.19,
   "text": "is when people get sick."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.64,
   "end": 7.02,
   "text": "Your fridge is humming again."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.34,
   "end": 8.62,
   "text": "The food feels cold."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.96,
   "end": 10.05,
   "text": "So people eat it."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.43,
   "end": 11.48,
   "text": "That's the mistake."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.84,
   "end": 16.63,
   "text": "The USDA says food in a fridge stays safe for only about four hours without power."
  },
  {
   "start": 16.93,
   "end": 18.73,
   "text": "After that, meat, milk,"
  },
  {
   "start": 18.89,
   "end": 20.72,
   "text": "eggs and leftovers have to go."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.1,
   "end": 22.26,
   "text": "Your freezer is different."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.54,
   "end": 25.28,
   "text": "If the food still has ice crystals, you can refreeze it."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.59,
   "end": 27.83,
   "text": "And never taste food to check if it's safe."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.16,
   "end": 29.84,
   "text": "The USDA's rule is simple:"
  },
  {
   "start": 30.22,
   "end": 30.81,
   "text": "when in doubt..."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.11,
   "end": 31.81,
   "text": "throw it out."
  },
  {
   "start": 32.33,
   "end": 34.91,
   "text": "So how does a dead power grid come back to life?"
  },
  {
   "start": 35.34,
   "end": 35.93,
   "text": "That's next."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.26,
   "end": 37.28,
   "text": "Follow for part eight."
  }
 ]
}